# Phase XX – Generate Report Refactoring, Team Key Migration & Commit Analysis Enhancements

## Objective

Refactor the Generate Report workflow to:

- Eliminate Project Key dependency.
- Standardize on Team Key across the application.
- Remove duplicate Scan Job implementation.
- Reduce GitHub API calls.
- Improve commit analysis accuracy.
- Introduce Commit Analysis metadata persistence.
- Simplify database model.
- Improve maintainability without changing existing functionality.

---

# Enhancement 1 – Replace Project Key with Team Key

## Background

Project Key represents only one project under a Team.

Release execution always happens at Team level.

Therefore Project Key must no longer participate in Generate Report processing.

---

## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-1.1

Remove `projectKey` from Generate Report request payload.

UI must never send Project Key.

---

### AC-1.2

ReportController.generateReport()

must no longer read Project Key.

---

### AC-1.3

Replace every Project Key usage with Team Key.

This includes:

- Controller
- Service
- Repository
- DTO
- Entity
- Database queries
- Cache
- Validation
- Report generation

---

### AC-1.4

Project Key should remain only where it is genuinely required for iTrack story retrieval.

No other module should depend on Project Key.

---

